00:42:51,161 --> 00:42:53,420
60 feet across a man-made lake.

522
00:42:56,460 --> 00:42:58,660
And, of course, there's old Bruce the Sharp.

523
00:42:58,661 --> 00:43:08,860
With so many hydraulic attractions, it's no surprise that even the trams at Universal

524
00:43:08,861 --> 00:43:13,020
run with the help of hydraulics.

525
00:43:13,021 --> 00:43:20,660
Whether it's entertainment or construction, when something big needs to be moved, hydraulics

526
00:43:20,661 --> 00:43:24,460
still remains the power of choice, at least for now.

527
00:43:24,461 --> 00:43:29,300
But the continuing advancement of electronic systems may eventually lead to electric motors

528
00:43:29,301 --> 00:43:35,100
replacing hydraulics as the power source leader in force applications.

529
00:43:35,101 --> 00:43:41,220
I believe the future of hydraulics is a combination of electronics and hydraulics.

530
00:43:41,221 --> 00:43:48,200
In some applications, hydraulics may be phased out, but we will never see the power density

531
00:43:48,201 --> 00:43:52,100
from the electronic systems that we see from the hydraulic system.

532
00:43:52,101 --> 00:43:58,460
I just can't fathom any other technology that will be able to generate hundreds of thousands

533
00:43:58,461 --> 00:44:04,380
of foot-pounds of torque or the thousands of tons of force needed to drill a hole in

534
00:44:04,381 --> 00:44:06,860
through a mountain or under a lake.

535
00:44:06,861 --> 00:44:14,420
Whether or not hydraulics is supplanted by another power application is yet to be decided.

536
00:44:14,421 --> 00:44:22,080
But until that day comes, when something big has to be moved, when a high amount of power

537
00:44:22,081 --> 00:44:30,800
is needed. With precision control, hydraulics will remain the power of choice.

538
00:44:52,080 --> 00:44:54,680
All right.

